// Service, support, control and recourse (L. 843-1/6, L. 844-1, L. 845-1/2/6).
//
// D1 fund duty to serve: «attribuée, servie et contrôlée, pour le compte
// de l'Etat, par les CAF et les MSA» (L. 843-1): the due quarterly
// amount is paid to the payee — bearer the serving fund (empirical
// link), performance the empirical prime_versee fact. State financing
// (L. 843-6) is not a modelled norm.
// Accompaniment (L. 844-1): a job-seeking payee has the right to adapted
// support — plain institutional right on the retained job-seeker fact.
// P1 control power (L. 845-1): fund directors control, investigate and
// sanction under the listed articles — holder the director (empirical),
// exercise the pronounced control/inquiry/sanction (empirical
// controle_prononce), effect the distinct institutional consequence
// controle_prend_effet (AAH AttributionCdaph pattern: an effect that
// re-produces its own exercise refuses execution under norm runtime
// completion on 0.2.7 — COMPARE PPA13 diagnosis, both engines).
// D2 information duty (L. 845-2 al. 3): the payee is informed of the
// claim/appeal routes — bearer the fund, maintain information_recours.
// Amicable appeal first, then the administrative court (al. 1-2):
// procedure, not modelled beyond D2.
// Paid intermediation to obtain the bonus is punished under L. 554-2
// (L. 845-6): the criminal scale is unmodelled; the retained
// intermediation fact derives the institutional offence flag.
//
// Scenarios: tests/devoirs-*.lawtest (positions: ACTIVE / power
// exercisable / offence flag / no right — no position).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.css.prime_activite version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:ppa";

use self::{
    CSS_L843_1_ED2021_01_01,
    CSS_L843_1_ED2021_03_25,
    CSS_L843_1_ED2021_06_01,
    CSS_L843_1_ED2022_03_21,
    CSS_L843_1_ED2023_12_31,
    CSS_L843_1_ED2024_01_01,
